    <floater.string name="tab_tip_home">Start here: the photo presets, brightness, blur and color tone, the sky and water, the shutter, Stop the World, the composition guide and the settings you starred.</floater.string>
    <floater.string name="tab_tip_quality">Set the overall quality and performance cost first: the quality level (seven levels, Low to Ultra), draw distance, object detail, cleaner photos; in Details, shading (GTAO), reflections, mirrors, water and anti-aliasing.</floater.string>
    <floater.string name="tab_tip_light">The sky, the water and the weather: lists of skies and water settings; the water mirror, your reflection and splashes; rain, wet ground and puddles, dripping eaves, rain on your umbrella, snow; ground fog, fireflies and light shafts. The tab scrolls.</floater.string>
    <floater.string name="tab_tip_color">The light and the colors: light direction, shadow depth, glare, lens flare and star rays; brightness, contrast, color tone and the looks (LUTs); in Details, how soft, far and fine shadows are, tone mapping, exposure and sharpness.</floater.string>
    <floater.string name="tab_tip_camera">The camera itself: field of view, tilt, background blur and depth of field, saved camera positions, the composition guide, camera movement and the 3D mouse.</floater.string>
    <floater.string name="tab_tip_subject">The avatar in the picture: softer face shadows, contact shadows (fingertips, feet), eyes that look at the camera and how far they and the head may turn, and hair that sways in the wind.</floater.string>
    <floater.string name="tab_tip_shoot">Taking the photo: its size and shape, the shutter, the last photo and its folder, the standard snapshot window, the file format and JPEG quality.</floater.string>
